{"tool_name":"speq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"speq","home":"http://github.com/sor8sh/SPEQ","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Quality Assessment of Peptide Tandem Mass Spectra with Deep Learning.","addition_date":"2022-06-10T08:36:32.595172Z","last_update_date":"2022-06-10T08:36:32.597950Z","tool_type":["Script"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:speq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"binma@uwaterloo.ca","name":"Bin Ma","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Soroosh Gholamizoj","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6283-6282"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3631"},{"term":"Protein identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3767"},{"term":"Spectrum calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3860"}]}],"name":"SPEQ","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAB874","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022 The Author(s) 2022. Published by Oxford University Press.Motivation: In proteomics, database search programs are routinely used for peptide identification from tandem mass spectrometry data. However, many low-quality spectra cannot be interpreted by any programs. Meanwhile, certain high-quality spectra may not be identified due to incompleteness of the database or failure of the software. Thus, spectrum quality (SPEQ) assessment tools are helpful programs that can eliminate poor-quality spectra before the database search and highlight the high-quality spectra that are not identified in the initial search. These spectra may be valuable candidates for further analyses. Results: We propose SPEQ: a spectrum quality assessment tool that uses a deep neural network to classify spectra into high-quality, which are worthy candidates for interpretation, and low-quality, which lack sufficient information for identification. SPEQ was compared with a few other prediction models and demonstrated improved prediction accuracy.","authors":[{"name":"Gholamizoj S."},{"name":"Ma B."}],"date":"2022-03-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"SPEQ: Quality assessment of peptide tandem mass spectra with deep learning"},"pmcid":"PMC8896601","pmid":"34978568"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Protein modifications","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0601"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SPEQ","home":"https://bio.tools/speq","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Quality Assessment of Peptide Tandem Mass Spectra with Deep Learning.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:speq/script/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":false,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":5,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab874","pmcid":"PMC8896601","pmid":"34978568","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"SPEQ: quality assessment of peptide tandem mass spectra with deep learning.","year":2022}]}],"readme":true,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":true,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects